+ rg -n 'KleanTarget|target|theorem|axiom|opaque|sorry|admit|unsafe' /reference/klean-generation/generated --glob '*.lean'
/reference/klean-generation/generated/Klean162StringToMd5/Prelude.lean:7:Currently we translate hooked functions as uninterpreted functions together with axioms asserting their behavior.
/reference/klean-generation/generated/Klean162StringToMd5/Prelude.lean:14:The behavior of the uninterpreted symbols can be asserted through axioms or theorems.
/reference/klean-generation/generated/Klean162StringToMd5/Prelude.lean:15:Inconsistencies can arise from them, so it falls under the user to make sure axioms are consistent and/or theorems provable.
/reference/klean-generation/generated/Klean162StringToMd5/Prelude.lean:18:With the theory defined through function rules, simplifications can be stated as theorems.
/reference/klean-generation/generated/Klean162StringToMd5/Prelude.lean:19:These theorems should be provable directly from the function rules and the semantics of the Sorts.
/reference/klean-generation/generated/Klean162StringToMd5/Prelude.lean:60:-- We use axioms to have uninterpreted functions
